cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the associated paper, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Möbius Galton Board"
abstract: >
  The first non-orientable Galton board. A classical Galton board whose
  left and right edges are identified via a Möbius seam produces a clean
  phase transition in the even-parity fraction at the information-theoretic
  constant k* = 1/(2 ln 2) ≈ 0.7213. Includes analytic theory, Monte Carlo
  validation, coherent-optical and single-photon quantum simulations,
  continuous waveguide model, Möbius collider extension, and physical
  build plans.
